---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site, isTodo } from '../config/site';
import { emailUrl, phoneUrl, whatsappUrl, withBase } from '../utils/links';

const contact = emailUrl('Privacy request') ?? phoneUrl() ?? whatsappUrl('privacy');
const hasContact = !isTodo(site.contact.email) || !isTodo(site.contact.phone) || !isTodo(site.contact.whatsappNumber);
const contactLabel = !isTodo(site.contact.email)
  ? site.contact.email
  : !isTodo(site.contact.phone)
    ? site.contact.phone
    : 'contact us';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How InnovaTech World collects and uses your personal data.">
  <article class="prose privacy">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 13 November 2026</p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains what personal data InnovaTech World ("we", "us"), based in
      {' '}{site.location}, collects through the InnovaTech World Knowledge Hub (the "Site"), why we
      collect it, and your rights. We follow the principles of Nigeria's Data Protection Act 2023
      (NDPA), overseen by the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (NDPC). By using the Site you agree
      to this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>We collect only what we need to run your training:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your <strong>name</strong> and <strong>email address</strong> - to create and secure your account.</li>
      <li>Your <strong>course progress</strong> - which lessons you complete.</li>
      <li>Your <strong>assignment submissions</strong> - the links you share and any notes - and the feedback and scores on them.</li>
      <li>Your <strong>attendance</strong> at mentoring sessions.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> collect home addresses, government ID numbers, or payment details
      through the Site, and we do not ask for sensitive personal data. Public pages (lessons,
      resources) can be read without an account and without signing in.
    </p>

    <h2>Chat assistant (Lulu)</h2>
    <p>
      Lulu is an automated site guide, not a human employee or generative AI. When you send a question,
      the Site searches published public pages and returns matching excerpts and links. The question is
      processed by the Site's Vercel-hosted endpoint; it is not sent to OpenAI or another AI provider.
      Each question is handled independently; no conversation history is sent to the endpoint. Do not
      send passwords, verification codes, payment details, student records, government IDs, or other
      sensitive information. Search results may be incomplete or out of date; verify important
      information with InnovaTech.
    </p>
    <p>
      InnovaTech does not save Lulu chat transcripts in the Site, Supabase, or your browser's local
      storage. Messages remain in the current page only and are cleared when you reload or leave it.
      Vercel processes the request and network information to provide the endpoint and may retain
      operational records under its current terms and settings. The Site's code does not send questions
      to an external AI service.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>
      To deliver your training: to give you access to your courses, track your progress, review your
      work, provide feedback, record attendance, and communicate with you about the programme. Our
      lawful bases under the NDPA are your <strong>consent</strong> (which you give on first login) and
      the <strong>performance of our training agreement</strong> with you.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p>
      Only <strong>you</strong> and your <strong>facilitator</strong>. Other students cannot see your
      data. This is enforced in the database itself through Row Level Security, not just in the website.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Your account and learning data are stored in <strong>Supabase</strong>, a secure hosted database
      service that acts as our data processor for this training. The website is hosted on
      <strong>Vercel</strong>. Both may process data on servers outside Nigeria; where that happens we
      rely on their security measures and standard contractual protections. We do not sell your data or
      share it with advertisers.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
    <p>
      We do not use advertising cookies or third-party trackers. The portal uses your browser's local
      storage and a secure session cookie only to keep you signed in and to remember preferences such
      as your theme and lesson progress. If we ever enable privacy-friendly analytics, we will update
      this policy first.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your account data for as long as you have an active account and for up to
      <strong>24 months</strong> after your last activity. After that we delete or anonymise it, unless
      we are required to keep it longer to meet a legal obligation. You can ask us to delete it sooner
      (see your rights below).
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the NDPA you can:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you;</li>
      <li>ask us to correct anything that is wrong (you can edit your name in <em>My Learning</em>);</li>
      <li>ask us to delete your data and close your account;</li>
      <li>withdraw your consent at any time;</li>
      <li>complain to the NDPC if you believe we have mishandled your data.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>When you ask us to delete your account, your profile, progress, submissions, feedback and attendance are removed.</p>

    <h2>Keeping your data safe</h2>
    <p>
      Passwords are stored securely (hashed) by our authentication provider - we never see them. Access
      to student data is limited to you and your facilitator. Please use a strong, unique password and
      keep it private.
    </p>

    <h2>Age</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is intended for people aged 16 and over. If you are under 16, please use it only with a
      parent or guardian's involvement.
    </p>

    <h2>Public features</h2>
    <p>
      Your name and progress are <strong>never</strong> shown publicly. The optional "student showcase"
      and "certificate verification" features display information only with your separate written
      permission.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. We will post the new version here and change the
      "last updated" date above. Significant changes will be communicated to enrolled students.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    {
      hasContact && contact ? (
        <p>
          To make a request or ask a question, contact us at <a href={contact}>{contactLabel}</a>
          {' '}or through our <a href={withBase('/contact/')}>contact page</a>.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>Please reach us through our <a href={withBase('/contact/')}>contact page</a>.</p>
      )
    }
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy { margin-inline: auto; }
  .privacy .muted { color: var(--color-muted); }
</style>
